// The enemy seat's demo box (`demo=enemy`, `src/lab/demo/enemy.rs`; Reports/teaching-the-colony-2026-10-25/enemy-seat-demo.md). The
// steady-income bed of the Teacher lane's `lab_mid_fruit` (no plants, mister off, 52 ants landing at column 256 on
// frame 6,000 on one tank), with the two fruit heaps 40 columns from the door instead of 75: the trained pool lives
// with food 10-50 columns out and starves at 100-240. Measured 2026-10-25 (`labsurvive founders=std`, no raider):
// alive at 66,000 frames on 4 of 4 seeds, 109 / 145 / 176 / 178 ants. The demo fast-forwards to 26,000 (the colony
// dug in), then sets the player's centipede down on the surface.
(
    name: "demo_enemy",
    title: "THE RAIDER",
    question: "You are a centipede. The colony bites back: can you raid its nest and get out alive, and what does it cost them?",
    bed: (
        width: 512,
        height: 320,
        soil_depth: 80,
        ground_y: 160,
        compartments: 1,
        founders: 0,
        species: "grass",
        colonies: 0,
        colony_ants: 52,
        colony_species: "ant",
        predators: 0,
        lamp_spacing: 33,
        seed: 1,
        extra_walls: [],
    ),
    settings: [
        (subject: "the bed", field: "rain", value: 0),
    ],
    placements: [],
    timeline: [
        (at: 6000, every: 0, until: 0, what: Colony(species: "ant", x: 256, count: 52)),
        (at: 5990, every: 0, until: 0, what: Heap(material: "fruit", x: 216, cells: 60)),
        (at: 5990, every: 0, until: 0, what: Heap(material: "fruit", x: 296, cells: 60)),
        (at: 6500, every: 500, until: 0, what: Heap(material: "fruit", x: 216, cells: 20)),
        (at: 6500, every: 500, until: 0, what: Heap(material: "fruit", x: 296, cells: 20)),
    ],
    horizon: 600000,
)
